insert into public.brand_size_charts
  (brand_key, brand_label, brand_match, department, garment, category_match, rows, note, source_url, confidence, verified, updated_by) values
  ('beyondyoga', 'Beyond Yoga', ARRAY['beyond yoga','beyondyoga']::text[], 'Women', 'Tops & outerwear', ARRAY['top','tank','tee','shirt','bra','hoodie','sweatshirt','dress','long sleeve','jacket','coat','outerwear','vest','cardigan']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS","measurements":{"bust":"31.5","waist":"25","numeric":"0"}},{"size":"XS","measurements":{"bust":"32-34","waist":"26-27.5","numeric":"0-2"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"bust":"34.5-36","waist":"28-29.5","numeric":"4-6"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"bust":"36.5-38","waist":"30-31.5","numeric":"8-10"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"bust":"38.5-40","waist":"32-33.5","numeric":"12-14"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"bust":"40.5-42","waist":"34-35.5","numeric":"16-18"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"bust":"42.5-45","waist":"36-39.5","numeric":"20-22"}},{"size":"1X","measurements":{"bust":"45-47","waist":"41-43","numeric":"18-20"}},{"size":"2X","measurements":{"bust":"48-51","waist":"44-47","numeric":"22-24"}},{"size":"3X","measurements":{"bust":"52-55","waist":"48-51","numeric":"26-28"}},{"size":"4X","measurements":{"bust":"56-60","waist":"52-56","numeric":"30-32"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'US-3290 added the SOURCE URL and widened this to outerwear: the rows were already the brand''s own and were re-checked against the live page in September 2026, and Beyond Yoga publishes ONE chart for everything it makes. ⚠ Its page ships the SAME table twice, the second captioned ''TEST NEW TABLE''. BODY measurements from the official guide (XXS-4X). Official rule: when bust and waist suggest two sizes, go with the BUST. WARNING — do NOT cross-use this waist column with the Bottoms chart: the two charts give different waists for the same alpha size and different alpha↔numeric maps. The map is NON-MONOTONIC across the standard/extended boundary (XXL=20-22 but 1X=18-20).', 'https://beyondyoga.com/pages/size-guide', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('reicoop', 'REI Co-op', ARRAY['rei co-op','rei coop','reicoop','rei']::text[], 'Men', 'Tops', ARRAY['top','jacket','coat','shell','hoodie','fleece','vest','rain jacket','shirt','long sleeve','tee','sweater','knit']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XS","measurements":{"chest":"35","sleeve":"32"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"36-38","sleeve":"32.5"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"39-41","sleeve":"33"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"42-45","sleeve":"33.5"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"46-49","sleeve":"34"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"chest":"50-53","sleeve":"34.75"}},{"size":"XXXL","measurements":{"chest":"54-57","sleeve":"35.5"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'US-3293 REPLACED the approximation that stood here with REI Co-op''s OWN chart, which runs XS-XXXL and adds sleeve length. ⚠ THE OLD ROWS WERE WRONG IN THE MIDDLE: they read L 42-45 correctly but S 35-38 and M 38-41 against a published 36-38 and 39-41, so both overlapped their neighbour by an inch. BODY inches — house-label shells carry layering room over this, so the chart does NOT predict the flat measurement. XS is a single 35in chest, not a range. The guide is a product-page modal (its /help/size-charts and /product-size-charts paths refuse a plain fetch entirely), which is why the source URL points at a trouser.', 'https://www.rei.com/product/236137/rei-co-op-trailmade-pants-mens', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('stssy', 'Stüssy', ARRAY['stussy','stüssy']::text[], 'Men', 'Apparel (US alpha ↔ numeric waist, body inches)', ARRAY['tee','t-shirt','shirt','top','hoodie','sweatshirt','crewneck','fleece','hooded','jacket','coat','outerwear','vest','bottom','pant','trouser','short','jean','chino']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XS / 28","measurements":{"chest":"38-40","waist":"26-27"}},{"size":"S / 29-30","measurements":{"chest":"42-44","waist":"28-29"}},{"size":"M / 31-32","measurements":{"chest":"44-46","waist":"30-31"}},{"size":"L / 33-34","measurements":{"chest":"46-48","waist":"32-34"}},{"size":"XL / 36","measurements":{"chest":"48-50","waist":"35-36"}},{"size":"XXL / 38","measurements":{"chest":"52-54","waist":"37"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Stüssy is US alpha sizing — no national cross-map applies, unlike BAPE in this same group. Cut relaxed/boxy by design, which is the intended silhouette and not a mislabel. These are body-equivalent figures for the nominal streetwear grade, not Stüssy-published specs. Measure the garment flat (chest across the underarm seam, doubled). NOTE vintage pieces were graded differently from current production, so on this brand especially the tag is a claim to check against the actual measurement. US-3289 REPLACED the old approximation with Stüssy''s OWN published chart, which is also why bottoms and outerwear now resolve: Stüssy prints ONE table carrying the alpha and the numeric waist together, so a Stüssy M top and a Stüssy 31 bottom are the same body.', 'https://www.stussy.com/pages/size-guide', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('reformation', 'Reformation', ARRAY['reformation']::text[], 'Women', 'Dresses & tops (US numeric)', ARRAY['dress','top','tee','shirt','blouse','knit','sweater','cardigan','jacket','long sleeve']::text[], $json$[{"size":"US 0","measurements":{"bust":"33","waist":"25","hip":"36"}},{"size":"US 2","measurements":{"bust":"34","waist":"26","hip":"37"}},{"size":"US 4","measurements":{"bust":"35","waist":"27","hip":"38"}},{"size":"US 6","measurements":{"bust":"36","waist":"28","hip":"39"}},{"size":"US 8","measurements":{"bust":"37.5","waist":"29.5","hip":"40.5"}},{"size":"US 10","measurements":{"bust":"39.5","waist":"31.5","hip":"42.5"}},{"size":"US 12","measurements":{"bust":"41.5","waist":"33.5","hip":"44.5"}},{"size":"US 14","measurements":{"bust":"45","waist":"37.5","hip":"47.5"}},{"size":"US 16","measurements":{"bust":"47","waist":"39.5","hip":"49.5"}},{"size":"US 18","measurements":{"bust":"49","waist":"41.5","hip":"51.5"}},{"size":"US 20","measurements":{"bust":"51","waist":"43.5","hip":"53.5"}},{"size":"US 22","measurements":{"bust":"53","waist":"45.5","hip":"55.5"}},{"size":"US 24","measurements":{"bust":"55","waist":"47.5","hip":"57.5"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Reformation is US women''s NUMERIC sizing (0-24) on a fitted, dress-led cut — no national cross-map applies (contrast Sézane in this same group, whose bare "38" is a US 6, not a US 38: the two look alike on a tag and are not). The house cut is close-fitting rather than relaxed, so a snug flat measurement is the intended silhouette and NOT a mislabel. These are body-equivalent figures US-3293 REPLACED the approximation with Reformation''s OWN numeric grade, which runs 0-24 rather than stopping at 12 and publishes a HIP column this chart did not have at all. Every value is a single number, not a range: the brand grades to a point. ⚠ THE RUN JUMPS AT 14 — bust goes 41.5 to 45 and waist 33.5 to 37.5, where every step below is two inches or less. That is the brand''s own extended-size break, not a transcription slip. Measure the garment flat (bust across the underarm seam, doubled). The STYLE NAME changes the price, not the fit — a Juliette and any other named dress in the same size are the same grade.', 'https://www.thereformation.com/fitting-and-sizes.html', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('oldnavy', 'Old Navy', ARRAY['old navy','oldnavy']::text[], 'Women', 'Tops, outerwear & dresses (alpha, RUNS LARGE)', ARRAY['top','tee','shirt','blouse','knit','sweater','sweatshirt','hoodie','tank','long sleeve','jacket','coat','outerwear','parka','vest','dress']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS / 000-00","measurements":{"bust":"30.5-31.5","waist":"22.25-24"}},{"size":"XS / 0-2","measurements":{"bust":"32.5-33.5","waist":"25-26"}},{"size":"S / 4-6","measurements":{"bust":"34.5-35.5","waist":"27-28"}},{"size":"M / 8-10","measurements":{"bust":"36.5-37.5","waist":"29-30"}},{"size":"L / 12-14","measurements":{"bust":"39-41","waist":"31.5-33.5"}},{"size":"XL / 16-18","measurements":{"bust":"43.5-46","waist":"36.25-39"}},{"size":"XXL / 20","measurements":{"bust":"48.75","waist":"42"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Old Navy RUNS LARGE — it is VANITY-SIZED (the value-tier pattern): an Old Navy M sits nearer a US L than the nominal grade suggests. Uniqlo in this SAME group runs the OPPOSITE way (a Uniqlo M is nearer a US 4-6) and both tags say only ''M'', which is exactly why the cross-map is in the size label. A garment that measures LARGER than its tag is NORMAL for this brand — it is the grade, not stretching, not a mislabel, and not a defect to grade down. US-3289 REPLACED the old approximation with Old Navy''s OWN published numbers, which is also why outerwear now resolves: Old Navy is on Gap''s chart platform and its plus file is literally named womenPlusTopsOuterwear, so its tops chart IS its outerwear chart. Petite repeats the same chest and waist, so that is a length class.', 'https://oldnavy.gap.com/customer-service/size-charts', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('woolrich', 'Woolrich', ARRAY['woolrich','john rich']::text[], 'Men', 'Outerwear, tops & bottoms', ARRAY['jacket','coat','outerwear','down','parka','shirt','wool','flannel','top','tee','sweater','knit','bottom','pant','trouser','short']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS (US XXXS)","measurements":{"chest":"32","waist":"26.75","hip":"32.25","sleeve":"32.5"}},{"size":"XS (US XXS)","measurements":{"chest":"33.75","waist":"28.75","hip":"34.25","sleeve":"32.75"}},{"size":"S (US XS)","measurements":{"chest":"35.75","waist":"30.75","hip":"36.25","sleeve":"33.75"}},{"size":"M (US S)","measurements":{"chest":"37.75","waist":"32.75","hip":"38.25","sleeve":"34.75"}},{"size":"L (US M)","measurements":{"chest":"40.25","waist":"35","hip":"40.5","sleeve":"35.5"}},{"size":"XL (US L)","measurements":{"chest":"42.5","waist":"37.5","hip":"43","sleeve":"36"}},{"size":"XXL (US XL)","measurements":{"chest":"45","waist":"39.75","hip":"45.25","sleeve":"36.5"}},{"size":"XXXL (US XXL)","measurements":{"chest":"47.25","waist":"42.25","hip":"47.75","sleeve":"37"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'BODY measurement — NOT flat-garment. WATCH THE SIZE SYSTEM, IT FOLLOWS THE ERA: this US alpha chart covers the American heritage wool (the Made-in-USA Buffalo Check era, mill closed 2018), but the ITALIAN-era outerwear sold under the same label may carry EU sizing instead — one brand, two systems, decided by which Woolrich the garment is. Confirm from the origin tag before trusting the label. The heritage wool is also cut GENEROUS/boxy as an overshirt layer, so the body chart does NOT predict the flat measurement. US-3290 REPLACED the old approximation with Woolrich''s OWN numbers. ⚠ WOOLRICH''S MEN''S LABELS RUN ONE SIZE LARGER THAN US, and its own conversion says so: Woolrich XXS = USA XXXS, XS = XXS, S = XS, M = S, L = M, XL = L, XXL = XL, XXXL = XXL. A Woolrich men''s L is a US M. That fact appears NOWHERE on any page the brand publishes under a size-chart URL — both of those return 200 with no table, and the US store is a separate Shopify shop on woolrich.us whose /pages/size-* paths 404. The working chart is the product page''s VIEW SIZE GUIDE drawer, published in centimetres; the inches here are converted from it.', 'https://woolrich.us/products/check-flannel-warren-shirt-grey-brown-check', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('woolrich', 'Woolrich', ARRAY['woolrich','john rich']::text[], 'Women', 'Outerwear, tops & bottoms', ARRAY['jacket','coat','outerwear','down','parka','shirt','wool','flannel','top','tee','sweater','knit','bottom','pant','trouser','short']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS","measurements":{"bust":"31.5","waist":"24.5","hip":"34.5","sleeve":"30"}},{"size":"XS","measurements":{"bust":"33","waist":"26","hip":"36.25","sleeve":"30.5"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"bust":"34.75","waist":"27.5","hip":"37.75","sleeve":"31"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"bust":"36.25","waist":"29.25","hip":"39.25","sleeve":"31.75"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"bust":"37.75","waist":"30.75","hip":"41","sleeve":"32.25"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"bust":"39.75","waist":"32.75","hip":"43","sleeve":"32.75"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"bust":"41.75","waist":"34.75","hip":"45","sleeve":"33.5"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'BODY measurement — NOT flat-garment. WATCH THE SIZE SYSTEM, IT FOLLOWS THE ERA: US alpha on the American heritage wool, possibly EU numbers on the Italian-era outerwear (the Arctic Parka) under the SAME label. Confirm which Woolrich the garment is from the origin tag before trusting the size. US-3290 REPLACED the old approximation with Woolrich''s OWN numbers, converted from the centimetres its product-page size drawer publishes. Unlike its MEN''S run, the women''s labels line up normally with US and UK — a Woolrich women''s XS is a UK 8 and an IT 40.', 'https://woolrich.us/products/12gg-cozy-wool-cash-crewneck-black', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('puma', 'PUMA', ARRAY['puma']::text[], 'Unisex', 'Apparel (alpha, body inches)', ARRAY['top','tee','shirt','jacket','track jacket','sweatshirt','hoodie','jersey','long sleeve','bottom','pant','trouser','short','jogger','legging','tight']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS","measurements":{"chest":"28.75-31.5","waist":"23.5-26.25","hip":"28.25-31"}},{"size":"XS","measurements":{"chest":"32-34.5","waist":"26.75-29.5","hip":"31.5-34.25"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"35-37.75","waist":"30-32.75","hip":"34.75-37.5"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"38.25-41","waist":"33-35.75","hip":"37.75-40.5"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"41.25-44.5","waist":"36.25-39.25","hip":"41-44"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"45-48.5","waist":"39.75-43.25","hip":"44.5-48"}},{"size":"2XL","measurements":{"chest":"48.75-52.25","waist":"43.75-47.75","hip":"48.5-52"}},{"size":"3XL","measurements":{"chest":"52.75-56.25","waist":"48-52","hip":"52.25-56"}},{"size":"4XL","measurements":{"chest":"56.75-60.25","waist":"52.25-56.25","hip":"56.25-60"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'BODY measurement (chest) — unlike the PUMA FOOTWEAR charts on this same brand: measure the flat chest (armpit to armpit) and DOUBLE IT. THIS IS THE GARMENT CHART. A size on a PUMA tag is a stamped shoe number OR an alpha chest letter depending on what the item is, and only the item type decides — a T7 track jacket reads here, a Suede reads on the footwear chart. Never carry one onto the other. US-3289 REPLACED the old approximation with PUMA''s OWN published numbers, which is also why bottoms now resolve. ⚠ PUMA''S US SIZE-CHARTS PAGE CARRIES NO BODY MEASUREMENTS AT ALL — all 21 of its tables are country conversions or how-to-measure captions. These are from PUMA''s AU site, which publishes CENTIMETRES only; the inches here are converted from its own columns. The men''s run is below; PUMA''s women''s chart is narrower at every size.', 'https://au.puma.com/au/en/sizecharts/sizecharts.html', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('reebok', 'Reebok', ARRAY['reebok']::text[], 'Unisex', 'Apparel (alpha, body inches)', ARRAY['top','tee','shirt','jacket','track jacket','sweatshirt','hoodie','jersey','long sleeve','bottom','pant','trouser','short','jogger','legging','tight']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XS","measurements":{"chest":"32.5-35","waist":"28-30.5","hip":"32-34.5"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"35-38","waist":"30.5-33","hip":"34.5-37.5"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"38-41","waist":"33-36","hip":"37.5-40.5"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"41-44.5","waist":"36-40","hip":"40.5-44"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"44.5-49","waist":"40-44.5","hip":"44-47.5"}},{"size":"2XL","measurements":{"chest":"49-53.5","waist":"44.5-49.5","hip":"47.5-51"}},{"size":"3XL","measurements":{"chest":"53.5-58","waist":"49.5-54.5","hip":"51-55"}},{"size":"4XL","measurements":{"chest":"58-62.5","waist":"54.5-59.5","hip":"55-59"}},{"size":"5XL","measurements":{"chest":"62.5-67","waist":"59.5-64.5","hip":"59-63"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'BODY measurement (chest) — unlike the Reebok FOOTWEAR charts on this same brand: measure the flat chest (armpit to armpit) and DOUBLE IT. THIS IS THE GARMENT CHART. A size on a Reebok tag is a stamped shoe number OR an alpha chest letter depending on the item, and only the item type decides. NOTE the runs-large caveat on the Reebok footwear charts is a FOOTWEAR fact and does NOT transfer here — the apparel is roughly true to size. US-3289 REPLACED the old approximation with Reebok''s OWN published chart. The rows below are its TOPS table; its BOTTOMS table is a separate chart on this brand because the two do not agree — a Reebok M top wants a 33-36in waist and a Reebok M bottom wants 32-35in. ⚠ /us/size-charts and /help/size_charts.html both 404; the working paths are under /pages/.', 'https://www.reebok.com/pages/unisex-clothing-size-guide', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('girlfriendcollective', 'Girlfriend Collective', ARRAY['girlfriend collective','girlfriendcollective']::text[], 'Women', 'Tops & bottoms (alpha XXS-6XL — the widest run in the KB)', ARRAY['top','tee','legging','pant','bottom','short','bra','sweatshirt','hoodie','dress','long sleeve','jacket','coat','outerwear','vest']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS","measurements":{"bust":"29-31","waist":"22-24","hip":"32-34"}},{"size":"XS","measurements":{"bust":"31-33","waist":"24-26","hip":"34-36"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"bust":"33-35","waist":"26-28","hip":"36-39"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"bust":"35-37.5","waist":"28-30.5","hip":"39-41.5"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"bust":"37.5-40.5","waist":"30.5-33","hip":"41.5-44"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"bust":"40.5-43","waist":"33-35.5","hip":"44-46.5"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"bust":"43-46.5","waist":"35.5-39","hip":"46.5-50"}},{"size":"XXXL","measurements":{"bust":"46.5-50","waist":"39-42.5","hip":"50-53.5"}},{"size":"4XL","measurements":{"bust":"50-53.5","waist":"42.5-46","hip":"53.5-57"}},{"size":"5XL","measurements":{"bust":"53.5-57","waist":"46-49.5","hip":"57-60.5"}},{"size":"6XL","measurements":{"bust":"57-60.5","waist":"49.5-53","hip":"60.5-64"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'US-3291 REPLACED the old approximation with Girlfriend Collective''s OWN published numbers, from its two guides (bust on the tops page, waist and hip on the bottoms page), and widened this to outerwear. ⚠ THE OLD ROWS WERE ABOUT AN INCH OFF AND DRIFTED FURTHER UP THE RUN — XXS read bust 30-32 where the brand publishes 29-31. The US numeric cross-map that used to sit in the size label is GONE, because the brand does not publish one; the label is now the brand''s own, including its XXXL spelling where this chart previously said 3XL. Girlfriend Collective is APPAREL ONLY (no footwear) and WOMEN''S ONLY, so no men''s chart is seeded rather than inventing one. THIS IS THE WIDEST SIZE RUN IN THE KNOWLEDGE BASE — XXS THROUGH 6XL — AND THAT IS THE POINT OF THE BRAND, not a footnote: a plus size here is a MAINLINE product, and the larger sizes are genuinely sought and are frequently the harder ones to find secondhand. TWO CONSEQUENCES. First, the letter spans a far wider range than a conventional brand''s, so an XL on this tag is NOT an XL on a brand whose run stops at XL — NEVER cross-map the letter between brands; read this chart or measure. Second, read the size off the tag exactly and state it. FIT: the Compressive fabric is a firm HIGH-COMPRESSION knit, so it fits tighter than an ordinary legging at the same letter by design — that is the product, not a mis-size. CONDITION, AND A FLAT PHOTO HIDES ALL OF IT: compressive knits fail by PILLING (inner thigh, under the seat) and by losing elastane recovery, which shows as a waistband that will not spring back and a fabric that goes SHEER WHEN STRETCHED. Check the high-abrasion zones and the stretch-sheerness explicitly and say what you found. Standard US alpha/numeric approximation — capped confidence.', 'https://girlfriend.com/pages/size-guide-tops', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('untuckit', 'UNTUCKit', ARRAY['untuckit']::text[], 'Women', 'Tops, bottoms, outerwear & dresses (ALPHA XS-XL)', ARRAY['top','shirt','blouse','dress','shirtdress','tee','sweater','jacket','coat','outerwear','vest','bottom','pant','trouser','short','jean']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XS","measurements":{"bust":"32.5-34.5","waist":"25.5-26.5","hip":"36-39"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"bust":"34.5-36.5","waist":"27.5-29.5","hip":"38-41"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"bust":"36.5-38.5","waist":"29.5-31.5","hip":"40-43"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"bust":"38.5-40.5","waist":"31.5-33.5","hip":"42-45"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"bust":"40.5-42.5","waist":"34.5-36.5","hip":"44-47"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'US-3290 added the SOURCE URL and widened this to bottoms and outerwear: the rows were already the brand''s own and re-checked against the live page in September 2026, and UNTUCKit publishes ONE women''s table headed ''Women’s Styles''. ⚠ /pages/size-guide, /pages/size-chart and /pages/mens-size-guide all 404; the working path is /pages/all-size-charts. UNTUCKit''s women''s line (launched 2017, driven by the fact that ~45% of the brand''s customers were women buying for men) runs ALPHA XS-XL; the waist column is the brand''s NATURAL waist. Brand-published. As with the men''s chart, NO BODY LENGTH is published, so the untucked-hem premise has no number to check against here either.', 'https://www.untuckit.com/pages/all-size-charts', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('johnnieo', 'Johnnie-O', ARRAY['johnnie-o','johnnieo','johnnie o']::text[], 'Men', 'Tops (ALPHA S-XXXL — body measurements)', ARRAY['top','tee','shirt','polo','sweater','hoodie','quarter zip','pullover','jacket','outerwear']::text[], $json$[{"size":"S","measurements":{"neck":"14-14.5","chest":"38-40","waist":"28-32","sleeve":"32-33"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"neck":"15-15.5","chest":"40-42","waist":"32-36","sleeve":"33-34"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"neck":"16-16.5","chest":"42-44","waist":"36-40","sleeve":"34-35"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"neck":"17-17.5","chest":"44-46","waist":"40-44","sleeve":"35-36"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"neck":"18-18.5","chest":"46-48","waist":"44-48","sleeve":"36-37"}},{"size":"XXXL","measurements":{"neck":"18.5-19","chest":"50-52","waist":"49-52","sleeve":"37-38"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Johnnie-O''s own published chart — BODY measurements, not flat-garment. ⚠ NOTE THE DISCONTINUITY, REPRODUCED FAITHFULLY: XXL chest ends at 48 and XXXL starts at 50 (and the waist jumps 48→49), so there is a gap in the brand''s own grade. It may be a brand-side typo — do NOT silently ''fix'' it; prefer the garment. Brand guidance is ''true to size'', sizing up if between sizes. US-3292 RETRACTS THE SENTENCE THAT USED TO SIT HERE, which said the standard bottoms chart could not be sourced. It could: Johnnie-O keeps its guides at /size-guide/<audience>-<group>, NOT under /pages/, which is why three earlier guesses 404''d. Bottoms, big & tall bottoms, women''s bottoms and boys'' bottoms are all separate charts now.', 'https://www.johnnie-o.com/size-guide/mens-tops', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('pendleton', 'Pendleton', ARRAY['pendleton']::text[], 'Men', 'Wool shirts & tops (alpha, CHEST inches)', ARRAY['shirt','top','board shirt','wool shirt','overshirt','jacket','tee','sweater','knit','coat','outerwear','vest','flannel']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XS","measurements":{"chest":"33-35","neck":"14","sleeve":"32-32.5"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"36-38","neck":"15","hip":"34-36","sleeve":"33-33.5"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"39-41","neck":"16","hip":"38-40","sleeve":"34-34.5"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"42-45","neck":"17","hip":"42-44","sleeve":"35-35.5"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"46-49","neck":"18","hip":"46-48","sleeve":"36-36.5"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"chest":"50-53","neck":"19","hip":"50-52","sleeve":"37-37.5"}},{"size":"3X","measurements":{"chest":"54-57","neck":"20","sleeve":"38-38.5"}},{"size":"4X","measurements":{"chest":"58-61","neck":"21","sleeve":"39-39.5"}},{"size":"5X","measurements":{"chest":"62-65","neck":"22","sleeve":"40-40.5"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'US-3293 REPLACED the approximation that stood here with Pendleton''s OWN chart, which runs XS-5X rather than S-XXL and adds hip and sleeve. ⚠ PENDLETON PUBLISHES A WAIST COLUMN IDENTICAL TO ITS CHEST COLUMN at every single size, which is not a body and is almost certainly a copy error on the brand''s table. The waist is therefore LEFT OUT rather than repeated as if it meant something; chest, neck, hip and sleeve are the columns to trust. ⚠ HIP IS BLANK at XS and at 3X-5X on the brand''s own table. The guide is a product-page modal, which is why the source URL points at a chino. ⚠ VINTAGE PENDLETON WOOL SHIRTS OFTEN RUN SMALLER / BOXIER than the modern alpha grid above (mid-century sizing + wool shrinkage) — measure the chest flat rather than trusting the tag''s alpha letter. ⚠ BLANKETS ARE NOT SIZED BY THIS CHART (fixed bed dimensions). Remember the tag ERA, not the size, drives vintage value.', 'https://www.pendleton-usa.com/product/mens-astoria-stretch-chinos/54360Z.html', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('orvis', 'Orvis', ARRAY['orvis']::text[], 'Men', 'Tops & outerwear (alpha, CHEST inches)', ARRAY['top','shirt','jacket','coat','vest','barn coat','field coat','tee','polo','sweater','knit','outerwear','flannel']::text[], $json$[{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"36","neck":"14.5","sleeve":"33"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"38-40","neck":"15-15.5","sleeve":"33.5-34"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"42-44","neck":"16-16.5","sleeve":"34.5-35"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"46-48","neck":"17-17.5","sleeve":"35.5-36"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"chest":"50-52","neck":"18-18.5","sleeve":"36.5-37"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'US-3293 REPLACED the approximation that stood here with Orvis''s OWN published grid, and added neck and arm length, which Orvis charts and this corpus did not carry. ⚠ THE OLD ROWS WERE WRONG FROM L UP: they read L 41-43 and XXL 47-49 where Orvis publishes 42-44 and 50-52, a full three inches out at the top of the run. ⚠ SMALL IS A SINGLE 36in CHEST, not a range. BODY inches. Field and barn coats are cut for layering and measure generously over this; measure the chest flat. Orvis also publishes garment-specific charts on individual product pages.', 'https://www.orvis.com/mens-clothing-size-information.html', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('skims', 'SKIMS', ARRAY['skims']::text[], 'Women', 'Apparel (alpha XXS-4X, body inches)', ARRAY['shapewear','bodysuit','loungewear','underwear','dress','top','tee','shirt','sweater','knit','hoodie','sweatshirt','cardigan','legging','brief','thong','tank','jacket','coat','outerwear','robe']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS / 00","measurements":{"bust":"30-31","waist":"23-24","hip":"31-34"}},{"size":"XS / 0-2","measurements":{"bust":"31.5-33.5","waist":"24-26","hip":"34-36.5"}},{"size":"S / 4-6","measurements":{"bust":"34-36","waist":"26.5-28.5","hip":"37-39"}},{"size":"M / 8-10","measurements":{"bust":"36.5-38.5","waist":"29-31","hip":"39.5-41.5"}},{"size":"L / 12-14","measurements":{"bust":"39-41","waist":"31.5-34.5","hip":"42-44"}},{"size":"XL / 16","measurements":{"bust":"41.5-44.5","waist":"35-38","hip":"44.5-47.5"}},{"size":"2X / 18-20","measurements":{"bust":"45-48","waist":"38.5-41.5","hip":"48-51"}},{"size":"3X / 22-24","measurements":{"bust":"48.5-52","waist":"42-45.5","hip":"51.5-55"}},{"size":"4X / 26-28","measurements":{"bust":"52.5-56","waist":"46-49.5","hip":"55.5-59"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'SKIMS is SIZE-INCLUSIVE (XXS-4X) and its fabric is COMPRESSIVE: the Fits Everybody/Sculpting lines fit snug, so size to the BODY measurement, not the flat garment (a Fits Everybody piece measures much smaller than the body it fits). Bust/waist/hip are the signals. THE FABRIC IS THE GRADE — a stretched-out, non-recovering piece is a defect. US-3289 REPLACED the old approximation with SKIMS'' OWN published chart, which is also why tops and outerwear now resolve — SKIMS publishes ONE body chart and applies it to everything it makes.', 'https://skims.com/pages/size-guides', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('cotopaxi', 'Cotopaxi', ARRAY['cotopaxi']::text[], 'Men', 'Apparel (US alpha, body inches)', ARRAY['jacket','fleece','vest','top','shirt','windbreaker','fuego','teca','down','shell','bottom','pant','trouser','short','jogger']::text[], $json$[{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"34-36.5","waist":"27-29.5","hip":"33-36","sleeve":"32-32.5","inseam":"32"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"37-40","waist":"30-33","hip":"36.5-39.5","sleeve":"33-33.5","inseam":"32"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"41-43.5","waist":"34-36.5","hip":"40-43","sleeve":"33.5-34","inseam":"32"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"44-47","waist":"37-40.5","hip":"44-46.5","sleeve":"34.5-35","inseam":"32"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"chest":"48-50.5","waist":"41-45.5","hip":"47-50","sleeve":"35-35.5","inseam":"32"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'US-3287 REPLACED the approximation that stood here with Cotopaxi''s OWN published numbers, which is also why bottoms now resolve: the brand publishes ONE chart per department covering everything it makes, hip and inseam included. Sourced from the UK site — cotopaxi.com''s /pages/sizing-charts redirects to the homepage and its /pages/sizing-information 404s, and uk.cotopaxi.com is the working copy of the same guide. ⚠ THE DEL DÍA colour blocking is ONE-OF-A-KIND (remnant fabric, the sewer picks the colours) — a wild colour block is the PRODUCT, not a flaw. On the Fuego down jacket the FILL LOFT is the grade (a flat or leaking baffle is a defect).', 'https://uk.cotopaxi.com/pages/sizing-information', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('cotopaxi', 'Cotopaxi', ARRAY['cotopaxi']::text[], 'Women', 'Apparel (US alpha, body inches)', ARRAY['jacket','fleece','vest','top','shirt','windbreaker','fuego','teca','down','shell','bottom','pant','trouser','short','legging','jogger']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XS","measurements":{"bust":"32-33.5","waist":"25-26.5","hip":"34-35.5","sleeve":"29.75-30","inseam":"30.5"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"bust":"34-35.5","waist":"27-28.5","hip":"36-37.5","sleeve":"30.25-30.75","inseam":"30.5"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"bust":"36-37.5","waist":"29-31","hip":"38-39.75","sleeve":"31-31.25","inseam":"30.5"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"bust":"38-40.5","waist":"31.5-33.5","hip":"40-42.75","sleeve":"31.5-32","inseam":"30.5"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"bust":"41-43.5","waist":"34-36.5","hip":"43-45.5","sleeve":"32.25-32.75","inseam":"30.5"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'US-3287 REPLACED the approximation that stood here with Cotopaxi''s OWN published numbers, which is also why bottoms now resolve. Sourced from the UK site; see the men''s chart for why. The women''s run stops at XL — Cotopaxi sells extended sizing under its own collection and publishes no chart for it. ⚠ THE DEL DÍA colour blocking is ONE-OF-A-KIND (remnant fabric) — a wild colour block is the PRODUCT. On the Fuego the FILL LOFT is the grade.', 'https://uk.cotopaxi.com/pages/sizing-information', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('rab', 'Rab', ARRAY['rab']::text[], 'Men', 'Apparel (UK/EU ↔ US alpha, body inches)', ARRAY['jacket','down','softshell','shell','fleece','top','tee','shirt','sweater','knit','hoodie','sweatshirt','pant','microlight','neutrino','kinetic','xenon']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS","measurements":{"chest":"34","waist":"27","sleeve":"32"}},{"size":"XS","measurements":{"chest":"35.5","waist":"28","sleeve":"33"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"37","waist":"30","sleeve":"33"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"40","waist":"32","sleeve":"34"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"43","waist":"34","sleeve":"35"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"46","waist":"36","sleeve":"36"}},{"size":"XXL (US XL)","measurements":{"chest":"48","waist":"38","sleeve":"36"}},{"size":"3XL (US XXL)","measurements":{"chest":"51","waist":"41","sleeve":"36.5"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'RAB IS A BRITISH BRAND — sizing is UK/EU referenced (a EU 50 ≈ US M), so the SYSTEM (UK/EU vs US alpha) is the signal; read the label. On a DOWN jacket (Microlight / Neutrino) the FILL LOFT and any leaking baffle are the grade — stitch-through (Microlight) vs box-wall (Neutrino) comp differently. US-3289 REPLACED the old approximation with Rab''s OWN published numbers. ⚠ RAB''S ALPHA AND THE US ALPHA DIVERGE AT THE TOP: what Rab calls XXL is a US XL and its 3XL is a US XXL. Both labels are on Rab''s page and both are in the size column here.', 'https://rab.equipment/us/help/sizing-guide-mens', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('rab', 'Rab', ARRAY['rab']::text[], 'Women', 'Apparel (UK/EU ↔ US alpha, body inches)', ARRAY['jacket','down','softshell','shell','fleece','top','tee','shirt','blouse','sweater','knit','hoodie','sweatshirt','pant','microlight','neutrino','kinetic','xenon']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS (US 0, UK 6)","measurements":{"bust":"31.5","waist":"25.5","hip":"34","sleeve":"30"}},{"size":"XS (US 0-2, UK 8)","measurements":{"bust":"33","waist":"27","hip":"35.5","sleeve":"30.5"}},{"size":"S (US 4-6, UK 10)","measurements":{"bust":"35","waist":"28","hip":"37.5","sleeve":"31"}},{"size":"M (US 8-10, UK 12)","measurements":{"bust":"37","waist":"30","hip":"39.5","sleeve":"32"}},{"size":"L (US 12, UK 14)","measurements":{"bust":"39","waist":"32","hip":"41.5","sleeve":"33"}},{"size":"XL (US 14, UK 16)","measurements":{"bust":"41","waist":"34","hip":"43.5","sleeve":"34"}},{"size":"XXL (US 16, UK 18)","measurements":{"bust":"43","waist":"36","hip":"45.5","sleeve":"34"}},{"size":"3XL (US 18, UK 20)","measurements":{"bust":"45.5","waist":"38.5","hip":"48","sleeve":"35"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'RAB IS A BRITISH BRAND — women''s sizing is UK/EU referenced (a UK 12 ≈ US M), so the SYSTEM (UK/EU vs US alpha) is the signal; read the label. On a down jacket the FILL LOFT + baffles are the grade. US-3289 REPLACED the old approximation with Rab''s OWN published numbers, which carry the US and UK sizes together — a Rab M is a US 8-10 and a UK 12.', 'https://rab.equipment/us/help/sizing-guide-womens', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
