  ('spanx', 'Spanx', ARRAY['spanx']::text[], 'Women', 'Tops & outerwear, plus (body inches)', ARRAY['top','tee','shirt','blouse','sweater','knit','hoodie','sweatshirt','tank','cardigan','jacket','coat','outerwear','blazer','vest']::text[], $json$[{"size":"1X / 18-20","measurements":{"bust":"43-46","waist":"36-39","hip":"45-48"}},{"size":"2X / 22-24","measurements":{"bust":"46-49","waist":"39-42","hip":"48-51"}},{"size":"3X / 26","measurements":{"bust":"49-52","waist":"42-45","hip":"51-54"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'The 1X-3X half of the same Spanx table. It continues the standard run rather than restarting it: 1X picks up exactly where XL stops.', 'https://spanx.kustomer.help/tops-sizing-guide-B1PJHBjjq', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('uniqlo', 'Uniqlo', ARRAY['uniqlo']::text[], 'Unisex', 'Outerwear (body inches)', ARRAY['jacket','coat','outerwear','parka','blouson','fleece','vest']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS","measurements":{"chest":"30.75-33"}},{"size":"XS","measurements":{"chest":"31.5-34.75"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"34.75-37.75"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"37.75-41"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"41-44"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"44-47.25"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"chest":"47.25-50.5"}},{"size":"3XL","measurements":{"chest":"50.5-53.5"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Uniqlo''s outerwear body chart, chest only, taken from a unisex blouson. The brand sizes most outerwear unisex now, which is why this is not split by department. Note XXS and XS overlap by more than two inches, which is Uniqlo''s own table.', 'https://www.uniqlo.com/us/en/products/E491096-000/00', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('uniqlo', 'Uniqlo', ARRAY['uniqlo']::text[], 'Unisex', 'Bottoms (inch-sized — the number IS the waist)', ARRAY['bottom','pant','trouser','short','jean','chino','cargo']::text[], $json$[{"size":"22inch","measurements":{"waist":"22"}},{"size":"23inch","measurements":{"waist":"23"}},{"size":"24inch","measurements":{"waist":"24"}},{"size":"25inch","measurements":{"waist":"25"}},{"size":"26inch","measurements":{"waist":"26"}},{"size":"27inch","measurements":{"waist":"27"}},{"size":"28inch","measurements":{"waist":"28"}},{"size":"29inch","measurements":{"waist":"29"}},{"size":"30inch","measurements":{"waist":"30"}},{"size":"31inch","measurements":{"waist":"31"}},{"size":"32inch","measurements":{"waist":"32"}},{"size":"33inch","measurements":{"waist":"33"}},{"size":"34inch","measurements":{"waist":"34"}},{"size":"35inch","measurements":{"waist":"35"}},{"size":"36inch","measurements":{"waist":"36"}},{"size":"38inch","measurements":{"waist":"38"}},{"size":"40inch","measurements":{"waist":"40"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Uniqlo labels most bottoms in inches and the number IS the waist — a ''32inch'' tag means a 32in waist, with no vanity offset in either direction. Uniqlo prints identical Body Size and Product Size tables for these, so there is no ease to reason about. The men''s run is 27-40 and skips 37 and 39; the unisex run starts at 22 and skips 31 and 33.', 'https://www.uniqlo.com/us/en/products/E482868-000/00', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('aimleondore', 'Aimé Leon Dore', ARRAY['aimé leon dore','aime leon dore','aimeleondore']::text[], 'Unisex', 'Bottoms (system conversion only — no body measurements)', ARRAY['bottom','pant','trouser','short','jean','chino','sweatpant']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XS","measurements":{"us":"28","eu":"44","jp":"1"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"us":"30","eu":"46","jp":"2"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"us":"32","eu":"48","jp":"3"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"us":"34","eu":"50","jp":"4"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"us":"36","eu":"52","jp":"5"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"us":"38","eu":"54","jp":"6"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'ALD publishes NO body chart. Every product''s Sizing panel carries garment specs for that garment alone, and they differ enough between styles to make a brand-level number dishonest: the Officer Pant lists a 29.5in relaxed waist at size 28 while the Elasticated Trouser lists 26in at XS. What IS brand-wide is this conversion, printed identically on every product, so that is all this chart claims.', 'https://www.aimeleondore.com/products/double-pleated-officer-pant-2', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
